@prefix :     <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ekg-concept: <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .
@prefix annotation: <https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#> .
@prefix ekg-shape: <https://ekgf.org/ontology/shape#> .
@base         <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#>
  rdf:type     owl:Ontology ;
  sh:declare [
      sh:prefix "ekg-concept" ;
      sh:namespace "https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#"^^xsd:anyURI
  ] ;
  owl:imports  rdf: , ekg-shape: ;
  rdfs:label   "Concept Ontology"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "Data element concepts, called concepts for short, describe logical data elements with all their various forms of physical manifestations, as business and technical terms, and their sightings. The scope includes individual data elements and compound data constructs such as whole classes and shapes. ManifestationOccurrence records each sighting: the artifacts in which a manifestation was found and, within a statement, the positions in which it appears."@en .

#################################################################
#    Object properties
#################################################################

:hasConcept
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range    :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:label    "has concept"@en .

:inConceptSet
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range    :ConceptSet ;
  rdfs:label    "in concept set"@en .

:hasManifestation
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range    :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label    "has manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "Links a concept to a concrete manifestation such as a business term, API parameter, SPARQL variable, OWL class, SHACL shape, SKOS concept, source-code identifier, table, or column."@en .

:concept
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  owl:inverseOf :hasManifestation ;
  rdfs:domain   :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:range    :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:label    "concept"@en .

:preferredManifestation
  rdf:type           owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasManifestation ;
  rdfs:domain        :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range         :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label         "preferred manifestation"@en .

:preferredBusinessTerm
  rdf:type           owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf :preferredManifestation ;
  rdfs:domain        :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range         :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label         "preferred business term"@en .

:preferredQueryParameterManifestation
  rdf:type           owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf :preferredManifestation ;
  rdfs:domain        :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range         :URIParameterManifestation ;
  rdfs:label         "preferred query parameter manifestation"@en .

:preferredResultColumnManifestation
  rdf:type           owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf :preferredManifestation ;
  rdfs:domain        :DataElementConcept ;
  rdfs:range         :SPARQLResultColumnManifestation ;
  rdfs:label         "preferred result column manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment       "The manifestation whose label is the concept's public response-column name — what the edge projector renders in place of the SPARQL projection variable (story-signature design)."@en .

:manifestationResource
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:range    rdfs:Resource ;
  rdfs:label    "manifestation resource"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "The RDF resource manifested by a technical manifestation, for example an OWL class, OWL property, SHACL shape, SKOS concept, datatype, named graph, table IRI, or external schema identifier."@en .

:occurrenceOf
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label    "occurrence of"@en .

:occursWithin
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty , owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:label    "occurs within"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "Links an observed manifestation occurrence to an occurrence that directly contains it in the same source context. A column occurrence can occur within a sheet occurrence, or a property-shape occurrence within a node-shape occurrence. Multiple containers are permitted; ancestor links are queried rather than inferred."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:sourceSystem
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    rdfs:Resource ;
  rdfs:label    "source system"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "The system in which this occurrence of a manifestation was observed, identified by a resource IRI. A source repository is not required; the same manifestation may occur in multiple systems."@en .

:foundIn
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    rdfs:Resource ;
  rdfs:label    "found in"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "Identifies an artifact in which this occurrence was sighted, such as a dataset, a dataset file, a statement template, a story implementation, a raw-data view or a code file. An occurrence can identify containing artifacts at several granularities, for example a statement template, the story implementation using it and the dataset including its file. Containment between occurrences uses occursWithin; path and position literals locate the sighting within an artifact."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:statementPosition
  rdf:type      owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    :StatementPosition ;
  rdfs:label    "statement position"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "Classifies a position in which this occurrence appears within a query or update statement, or within a statement template rendering one, identified through foundIn. One appearance can have several positions, such as a parameter appearing in a graph pattern. The position is evidence about the statement; it does not declare a story's concept usage."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:templateLanguage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range :TemplateLanguage ;
  rdfs:label "template language"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Identifies the documented template language or substitution profile of a template document or placeholder manifestation. This general metadata property imposes no domain; each resource kind constrains its own language cardinality."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

#################################################################
#    Data properties
#################################################################

:manifestationValue
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label    "manifestation value"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "The exact lexical value for a manifestation when it is not naturally represented as an RDF resource. Examples: customerId, ?customer, _abc22, a SQL column token, or a Cypher identifier."@en .

:sourceRepository
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:anyURI ;
  rdfs:label    "source repository"@en .

:sourcePath
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label    "source path"@en .

:sourceLine
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label    "source line"@en .

:sourceColumn
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label    "source column"@en .

:sourceCommit
  rdf:type      owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain   :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:range    xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label    "source commit"@en .

#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

:DataElementConcept
  rdf:type      owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label    "Data Element Concept"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    """A logical data element with all its various forms of physical manifestations and their sightings. Called a concept for short.

The concept resource identifies the reusable meaning. Its manifestations record how that meaning is expressed, as business terms or as technical terms of many kinds, such as API parameters, SPARQL variables, template placeholders, OWL classes, SHACL shapes, table columns and source-code identifiers. ManifestationOccurrence resources record where each manifestation was observed physically: the systems and artifacts, such as datasets, files, statements and story implementations, in which it was sighted, and the positions in which it appears within a statement. The meaning, its manifestations and their occurrences keep separate identities; renaming a term or recording another sighting does not create a new concept.

This class follows the distinction between meaning and representation in ISO/IEC 11179, while extending beyond its object-class/property combinations to encompass compound data constructs. Manifestations may include business terms, programming-language identifiers, query variables, whole OWL classes, or SHACL shapes.

Reuse across contexts is encouraged. A concept is not inherently scoped to a particular context, although separate concepts may be created where needed. Independently created concepts may later be merged when their owners establish that they represent the same meaning. The concept identifies the shared meaning; its manifestations and graph relationships express and describe that meaning."""@en ;
  rdfs:seeAlso  <https://www.iso.org/standard/78925.html> ;
  dct:created   "2020-04-22T17:56:44Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

:ConceptSet
  rdf:type      owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label    "Concept Set"@en ;
  rdfs:comment  "A governed set of related data element concepts."@en .

:ConceptManifestation
  rdf:type      owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label    "Concept Manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "A business or technical expression of a data element concept: a human term, abbreviation, synonym, API parameter, variable name, RDF resource, OWL class, OWL axiom, SHACL shape, SKOS concept, table, column, or source-code identifier. Its appearances in sources are recorded as ManifestationOccurrence instances."@en .

:BusinessTerm
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Business Term"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "A human-facing manifestation such as a preferred label, synonym, or abbreviation."@en .

:Abbreviation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label       "Abbreviation"@en .

:FullSingularBusinessTerm
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label       "Full Singular Business Term"@en .

:FullPluralBusinessTerm
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label       "Full Plural Business Term"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "The plural noun form of a concept's business term — what a column header or collection heading shows."@en .

:Tagline
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label       "Tagline"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "A short subtitle or tagline shown beneath a concept's title."@en .

:Description
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :BusinessTerm ;
  rdfs:label       "Description"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "A longer human-facing description of a concept — hover text, tooltips, and detail panes."@en .

:TechnicalManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Technical Manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "A machine-facing manifestation such as an API token, query variable, code identifier, RDF resource, schema object, table, or column."@en .

:URIParameterManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "URI Parameter Manifestation"@en .

:SPARQLVariableManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SPARQL Variable Manifestation"@en .

:SPARQLResultColumnManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SPARQL Result Column Manifestation"@en .

:TemplateParameterManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation , [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :templateLanguage ;
    owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
  ] , [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :templateLanguage ;
    owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
  ] ;
  rdfs:label       "Template Parameter Manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "A concept's appearance as a placeholder in a statement template. A template processor substitutes validated input values before the resulting statement is parsed and executed. The template language determines the token syntax; its spelling alone does not identify a language or a native query variable."@en .

:TemplateLanguage a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Template Language"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A documented template language or substitution profile defining how a template document is interpreted. Its identity is distinct from a renderer implementing it and from the language of the rendered output. Declaring a profile does not approve it for execution."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:OWLClassManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "OWL Class Manifestation"@en .

:OWLPropertyManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "OWL Property Manifestation"@en .

:OWLAxiomManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "OWL Axiom Manifestation"@en .

:OWLNamedIndividualManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "OWL Named Individual Manifestation"@en .

:SHACLShapeManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SHACL Shape Manifestation"@en .

:SHACLShapeSetManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SHACL Shape Set Manifestation"@en .

:SKOSConceptManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SKOS Concept Manifestation"@en .

:SKOSConceptSchemeManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SKOS Concept Scheme Manifestation"@en .

:LiteralDatatypeManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Literal Datatype Manifestation"@en .

:RDFPredicateManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "RDF Predicate Manifestation"@en .

:RDFSClassManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "RDFS Class Manifestation"@en .

:RawSourceFieldManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Raw Source Field Manifestation"@en .

:SQLTableManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SQL Table Manifestation"@en .

:SQLColumnManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "SQL Column Manifestation"@en .

:CypherIdentifierManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Cypher Identifier Manifestation"@en .

:SourceCodeIdentifierManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Source Code Identifier Manifestation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment     "An identifier in a programming language, such as a variable, field, function, or class name. Use this class directly for languages without a dedicated subclass. manifestationValue records the exact identifier; ManifestationOccurrence records where it appears."@en .

:JavaScriptIdentifierManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :SourceCodeIdentifierManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "JavaScript Identifier Manifestation"@en .

:PythonIdentifierManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :SourceCodeIdentifierManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Python Identifier Manifestation"@en .

:JavaIdentifierManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :SourceCodeIdentifierManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "Java Identifier Manifestation"@en .

:JSONFieldManifestation
  rdf:type         owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf  :TechnicalManifestation ;
  rdfs:label       "JSON Field Manifestation"@en .

:ManifestationOccurrence
  rdf:type      owl:Class ;
  owl:disjointWith :DataElementConcept , :ConceptManifestation ;
  rdfs:label    "Manifestation Occurrence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "A concrete sighting of a concept manifestation in a system, source repository, dataset, statement, RDF file, OWL file, SHACL file, SPARQL query, SQL statement, Cypher statement, story implementation, or code file. foundIn identifies the artifacts in which it was sighted, and statementPosition classifies its positions within a statement."@en .

:StatementPosition
  rdf:type      owl:Class ;
  owl:disjointWith :DataElementConcept , :ConceptManifestation , :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  rdfs:label    "Statement Position"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "A classification of a syntactic position in which a manifestation occurrence appears within a query or update statement, or within a statement template rendering one. Positions classify observed appearances; they do not declare a story's concept usages. The built-in positions are ParameterPosition, ProjectionPosition, GraphTemplatePosition and GraphPatternPosition. Applications can define further positions as labeled and defined IRIs."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:ParameterPosition
  rdf:type      owl:NamedIndividual , :StatementPosition ;
  owl:differentFrom :ProjectionPosition , :GraphTemplatePosition , :GraphPatternPosition ;
  rdfs:label    "Parameter"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "An appearance whose value is supplied for an invocation rather than matched or produced by the statement: a template placeholder substituted before the statement is parsed, or a statement variable that the executing service pre-binds under its documented binding profile. Spelling does not establish this position; SPARQL treats $name and ?name as the same variable."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:ProjectionPosition
  rdf:type      owl:NamedIndividual , :StatementPosition ;
  owl:differentFrom :GraphTemplatePosition , :GraphPatternPosition ;
  rdfs:label    "Projection"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "An appearance as a result the statement returns: a variable or expression alias projected by its SELECT clause, or a DESCRIBE target. A projection inside a subquery belongs to the enclosing graph pattern, not to the statement's results."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:GraphTemplatePosition
  rdf:type      owl:NamedIndividual , :StatementPosition ;
  owl:differentFrom :GraphPatternPosition ;
  rdfs:label    "Graph Template"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "An appearance in a graph template whose instantiations the statement returns or adds: a CONSTRUCT template, an INSERT template, or INSERT DATA. This is the statement's own SPARQL graph template, not a template document in a template language. Terms in DELETE templates and DELETE DATA are not classified by this position."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:GraphPatternPosition
  rdf:type      owl:NamedIndividual , :StatementPosition ;
  rdfs:label    "Graph Pattern"@en ;
  rdfs:comment
    "An appearance in the graph pattern that the statement matches against data: its WHERE clause, including filters, bindings, inline data, optional, union, negation and subquery patterns, and the solution modifiers applied to those solutions."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .


#################################################################
#    Documentation annotations
#################################################################

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#Abbreviation>
    rdfs:comment "A shortened business term used as a business-language manifestation of a data element concept."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#BusinessTerm>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#ConceptManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#ConceptSet>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#CypherIdentifierManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an identifier in Cypher source or queries. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#DataElementConcept>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#Description>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#FullPluralBusinessTerm>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#FullSingularBusinessTerm>
    rdfs:comment "A business term expressing the full name of a data element concept in singular form."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#JSONFieldManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a field in a JSON document or interface. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#JavaIdentifierManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an identifier in Java source code. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#JavaScriptIdentifierManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an identifier in JavaScript source code. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#LiteralDatatypeManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a literal datatype. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#ManifestationOccurrence>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#OWLAxiomManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an OWL axiom. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#OWLClassManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an OWL class. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#OWLNamedIndividualManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an OWL named individual. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#OWLPropertyManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an OWL property. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#PythonIdentifierManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an identifier in Python source code. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#RDFPredicateManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a predicate used in RDF statements. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#RDFSClassManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through an RDFS class. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#RawSourceFieldManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a field in captured raw source data. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SHACLShapeManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a SHACL shape. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SHACLShapeSetManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a collection of SHACL shapes. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SKOSConceptManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a SKOS concept. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SKOSConceptSchemeManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a SKOS concept scheme. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SPARQLResultColumnManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a column in a SPARQL query result. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SPARQLVariableManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a variable in a SPARQL statement. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SQLColumnManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a column in a relational database schema. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SQLTableManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a table in a relational database schema. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#SourceCodeIdentifierManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#Tagline>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#TechnicalManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#TemplateParameterManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#URIParameterManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "A technical manifestation expressing a data element concept through a URI parameter in an interface. The manifestation is distinct from the reusable meaning of the concept and from its occurrences in source files."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#concept>
    rdfs:comment "Identifies the data element concept expressed by a concept manifestation; it is the inverse of hasManifestation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#hasConcept>
    rdfs:comment "Associates a resource with a data element concept. It does not impose a domain on the resource using the concept."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#hasManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#inConceptSet>
    rdfs:comment "Associates a data element concept with a concept set containing it."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#manifestationResource>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#manifestationValue>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#occurrenceOf>
    rdfs:comment "Identifies the concept manifestation that occurs at a particular source location."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#preferredBusinessTerm>
    rdfs:comment "Identifies a preferred business-language term for a data element concept."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#preferredManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "Identifies a preferred manifestation of a data element concept, specializing hasManifestation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#preferredQueryParameterManifestation>
    rdfs:comment "Identifies a preferred URI-parameter manifestation for a data element concept."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#preferredResultColumnManifestation>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourceColumn>
    rdfs:comment "Records the column position of a manifestation occurrence in its source. The ontology does not specify whether the position is zero-based or one-based."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourceCommit>
    rdfs:comment "Records the source repository commit associated with a manifestation occurrence."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourceLine>
    rdfs:comment "Records the line position of a manifestation occurrence in its source. The ontology does not specify whether the position is zero-based or one-based."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourcePath>
    rdfs:comment "Records the source path at which a manifestation occurrence is located."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourceRepository>
    rdfs:comment "Records the repository IRI associated with a manifestation occurrence as an xsd:anyURI literal."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#sourceSystem>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

#################################################################
#    Occurrence containment validation
#################################################################

:OccurrenceContainmentShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetSubjectsOf :occursWithin ;
  sh:targetObjectsOf :occursWithin ;
  sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
  sh:class :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  sh:not [ sh:or (
    [ sh:class :DataElementConcept ]
    [ sh:class :ConceptManifestation ]
  ) ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path :occursWithin ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:class :ManifestationOccurrence
  ] ;
  sh:sparql [
    sh:message "Occurrence containment must be acyclic; an occurrence cannot contain itself directly or through other occurrences."@en ;
    sh:select """
      PREFIX concept: <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#>
      SELECT $this WHERE {
        $this concept:occursWithin+ $this .
      }
    """
  ] ;
  rdfs:label "Occurrence Containment Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Validates resource-valued occurrence endpoints, separation from concepts and manifestations, and acyclic direct containment. Parent links are optional and may be multiple. Source-context correctness remains an observation made by the source analyzer."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

#################################################################
#    Sighting source and position validation
#################################################################

:OccurrenceSightingShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetSubjectsOf :foundIn , :statementPosition ;
  sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
  sh:class :ManifestationOccurrence ;
  sh:not [ sh:or (
    [ sh:class :DataElementConcept ]
    [ sh:class :ConceptManifestation ]
  ) ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path :foundIn ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:not [ sh:or (
      [ sh:class :ManifestationOccurrence ]
      [ sh:class :DataElementConcept ]
      [ sh:class :ConceptManifestation ]
      [ sh:class :StatementPosition ]
    ) ] ;
    sh:message "foundIn must identify an artifact resource, not a literal, occurrence, concept, manifestation or statement position. Containment between occurrences uses occursWithin."@en
  ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path :statementPosition ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
    sh:class :StatementPosition ;
    sh:message "statementPosition must identify a StatementPosition IRI."@en
  ] ;
  sh:sparql [
    sh:message "An occurrence with a statement position must identify, through foundIn, an artifact containing that statement."@en ;
    sh:select """
      PREFIX concept: <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#>
      SELECT $this WHERE {
        $this concept:statementPosition ?position .
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this concept:foundIn ?artifact }
      }
    """
  ] ;
  rdfs:label "Occurrence Sighting Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Validates where an occurrence was found and the positions in which it appears. Artifacts are resources distinct from occurrences, concepts, manifestations and positions; positions are StatementPosition IRIs; and a positioned occurrence identifies at least one containing artifact. Both properties remain optional for other occurrences."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:StatementPositionShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass :StatementPosition ;
  sh:targetObjectsOf :statementPosition ;
  sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
  sh:not [ sh:or (
    [ sh:class :DataElementConcept ]
    [ sh:class :ConceptManifestation ]
    [ sh:class :ManifestationOccurrence ]
  ) ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path rdfs:label ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ; sh:minLength 1
  ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path rdfs:comment ; sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ; sh:minLength 1
  ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path annotation:markdownDescription ; sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ; sh:minLength 1
  ] ;
  sh:or (
    [ sh:property [ sh:path rdfs:comment ; sh:minCount 1 ] ]
    [ sh:property [ sh:path annotation:markdownDescription ; sh:minCount 1 ] ]
  ) ;
  rdfs:label "Statement Position Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Requires a statement position to be an IRI with a nonempty literal label and a nonempty literal definition in rdfs:comment or markdownDescription, distinct from concepts, manifestations and occurrences. Covers built-in and application-defined positions."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

#################################################################
#    Template metadata validation
#################################################################

:TemplateParameterManifestationShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass :TemplateParameterManifestation ;
  sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path :templateLanguage ;
    sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ; sh:class :TemplateLanguage
  ] ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path :manifestationValue ;
    sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ;
    sh:datatype xsd:string ; sh:minLength 1
  ] ;
  rdfs:label "Template Parameter Manifestation Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Requires a template-placeholder manifestation to identify its language and its exact nonempty token. A shared token is interpreted within that language, not from its punctuation alone."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:TemplateLanguageShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass :TemplateLanguage ;
  sh:targetObjectsOf :templateLanguage ;
  sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
  sh:property [ sh:path rdfs:label ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ; sh:minLength 1 ] ;
  sh:property [ sh:path rdfs:seeAlso ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ] ;
  rdfs:label "Template Language Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Requires a stable language/profile IRI, a human-readable name, and a reference to its documentation. These metadata do not certify renderer behavior or execution approval."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

:LegacyTemplateManifestationShape a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass :LegraDollarManifestation ;
  sh:not [ sh:class :LegraDollarManifestation ] ;
  sh:message "LegraDollarManifestation is retired. Replace that type with TemplateParameterManifestation and declare its documented templateLanguage profile."@en ;
  rdfs:label "Legacy Template Manifestation Shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Rejects instances of the retired product-specific template-placeholder class, including instances also given the current type or a language. Migration must remove the retired type and identify the placeholder's language profile."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> a sh:ShapesGraph .

:ValidationShapeSet a owl:NamedIndividual , ekg-shape:ShapeSet ;
  ekg-shape:hasShapesGraph <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> ;
  rdfs:label "Concept Validation Shapes"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Validates occurrence containment, where occurrences were found and their statement positions, and template-placeholder metadata, including documented template-language profiles and rejection of retired template-placeholder classifications."@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#> ;
  ekg-shape:shapePurpose ekg-shape:Validation ;
  ekg-shape:hasShape :TemplateParameterManifestationShape , :TemplateLanguageShape ,
                     :LegacyTemplateManifestationShape , :OccurrenceContainmentShape ,
                     :OccurrenceSightingShape , :StatementPositionShape .

#################################################################
#    Markdown explanations
#################################################################

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/concept#>
    annotation:markdownDescription """
# Shared meanings, usage, and manifestations

A data element concept identifies reusable meaning. A story's concept usage
records how that story uses the meaning. A manifestation expresses the meaning
in business language or a technical system. These resources serve different
purposes and retain separate identities.

The [Story Ontology](https://ekgf.org/ontology/story#) declares the
input, output, and dependent usage model and its validation shapes. The
[Use Case Ontology](https://ekgf.org/ontology/use-case#) describes concept-set
ownership. Together these distinguish the story-owned usage from the shared
concept and its vocabulary membership.

## Vocabulary class labels

Classes in this ontology have English title-case `rdfs:label` values, such as
`Data Element Concept` and `Business Term`. Labels preserve acronyms such as
OWL, RDF, SHACL and SPARQL, and language names such as JavaScript. These labels
name the vocabulary classes. Business-term manifestations supply the names
used for individual concepts in their business languages and contexts.
"""@en .

:DataElementConcept annotation:markdownDescription """
## Meaning, manifestations and sightings

A data element concept describes a logical data element in three layers:

| Layer | Resource | Answers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Meaning | `DataElementConcept` | What does the data element mean? |
| Manifestation | `ConceptManifestation` | How is it expressed, as a business term or as one of many kinds of technical term? |
| Sighting | `ManifestationOccurrence` | Where was each manifestation observed physically, and in which statement position? |

For example, one concept can manifest as the business term "Product category",
as a `product_category` column in a dataset and as a placeholder in a story's
statement template. Each observed appearance is a separate occurrence:
`foundIn` identifies the dataset, file, template or story implementation, and
`statementPosition` records how the appearance is used within a statement.
These sightings are the evidence of how and where the logical data element
manifests physically. The concept keeps its identity when terms are renamed
or new sightings are recorded.

## Reuse across stories

For example, a customer-identifier concept can be an input to one story and an
output from another. Both stories reference the same data element concept.
Each story owns a separate usage object describing how it uses that concept.
Requiredness and server provision describe an input usage, rather than the
reusable meaning.

## Vocabulary membership and ownership

`inConceptSet` links a concept to its vocabularies. A use case owns a concept
set through `ekg-use-case:ownsConceptSet`. Stories select concepts from their
use case's own vocabularies and those inherited from ancestor use cases.
Referencing a concept does not give the story ownership of the concept.

## Manifestations

A business term, an API name, and a SPARQL variable can express the same
concept in different ways. `ConceptManifestation` resources record those
expressions, and `ManifestationOccurrence` resources record their appearances
in sources. A compound concept may also have a whole OWL class or SHACL shape
as a manifestation.

Reuse one manifestation for the same expression of the same concept within
the same language across story implementations; record individual appearances
as occurrences. For
example, twenty statement templates using `$m` as a placeholder for the same
meaning can reference one `TemplateParameterManifestation` with label and
`manifestationValue` `"$m"`. Its appearances in the template sources are
separate occurrences. The manifestation's `templateLanguage` identifies
the syntax in which that token is a placeholder. Native SPARQL variables use
`SPARQLVariableManifestation`. SPARQL itself permits dollar-prefixed query
variables, so the template language and the expression's role determine
the distinction; spelling alone does not establish it or shared meaning.

The template processor must use a documented, explicitly supported language
profile. For SPARQL value substitution, validated inputs must be serialized
as RDF terms for their intended positions, rather than copied as arbitrary
query fragments. The rendered statement must be parsed before execution.
The generic manifestation class neither selects an engine nor certifies
that an engine or its output is safe.

`occursWithin` links one observed occurrence to another, preserving the context
in which an attribute manifestation appears within a compound manifestation.
The same attribute concept can occur in different compounds in different
sources; containment belongs to the occurrence records, not to the shared
concepts or manifestations. A Story's concept usages declare its contract;
occurrences record observed appearances. Neither side is inferred from the other.
See the [occurrence containment guide](https://github.com/EKGF/ekg-ontologies/blob/main/docs/occurrence-containment.md)
for an executable example and the limits of declaration/observation comparisons.

`TemplateLanguage` identifies the source language/profile, not its renderer
or its generated output language. A template targeting SPARQL is still a
document in the declared template language until rendered. The
[SPARQL Story Implementation Ontology](https://ekgf.org/ontology/story-impl-sparql#)
declares template documents, renderers, and their implementation relationships.

## Template-placeholder migration

`LegraDollarManifestation` is retired. Replace that type assertion with
`TemplateParameterManifestation` and declare the manifestation's documented
`templateLanguage` profile. Keep the manifestation's identity, token, concept
links, and occurrence references. Do not infer its language from the `$`
prefix. `LegacyTemplateManifestationShape` rejects the retired classification
even when the current type and a language are also present.

See the [Method's concept-vocabulary documentation](https://method.ekgf.org/concept/concept/concept-vocabulary/#ontology).
"""@en .

:occursWithin annotation:markdownDescription """
## Observed direct containment

Links a ManifestationOccurrence to an occurrence directly containing it in the
same observed source context. For example, a column occurrence can be contained
in a worksheet occurrence. Following each endpoint's `occurrenceOf` and concept
links then relates the observed attribute meaning to the observed compound
meaning in that context.

Both endpoints are occurrences, not DataElementConcepts or ConceptManifestations.
One occurrence can have several observed containers, and a container can have
several children. This property is neither functional nor inverse-functional;
shared endpoints do not merge identities. It is irreflexive and not transitive.
Query `occursWithin+` to walk to all ancestors; the ontology does not materialize
indirect ancestors as direct containment assertions.

An analyzer must establish and assert containment from the source structure.
Matching paths, positions, types or manifestation identities do not create a
link. A referenced definition and a reference to it are different source
occurrences. Source-location and provenance properties remain on the observed
occurrences; containment does not copy or inherit those values.

OccurrenceContainmentShape checks resource endpoints, occurrence roles and
cycles. It does not read source content or prove that the asserted endpoints
share the same source context. See the
[containment guide](https://github.com/EKGF/ekg-ontologies/blob/main/docs/occurrence-containment.md)
for validation and queries.
"""@en .

:ManifestationOccurrence annotation:markdownDescription """
## An observed appearance

An occurrence records where a manifestation was observed. `occurrenceOf`
identifies the manifestation. `foundIn` identifies the artifacts containing the
sighting, such as a dataset, file, statement template or story implementation.
Repository, system, path, commit and line/column metadata locate it further.
Separate appearances of the same manifestation have separate occurrence
records. An occurrence is disjoint from the reusable DataElementConcept and
ConceptManifestation roles.

The manifestation's class records how the concept appears, for example as a
raw source field or a template placeholder. Within a query or update statement,
`statementPosition` records the role of the appearance: a parameter, a
projected result, a graph-template term or a graph-pattern term.

`occursWithin` records observed direct containment between occurrences.
Containment is optional, may have several parents, and must be acyclic.
Validate a coherent source/version context. A source analyzer is responsible
for identifying that context and determining the actual structure. Paths and
line/column literals alone do not identify a source artifact or source span;
`foundIn` links the sighting to resources representing its artifacts.

Observing a manifestation in a shape specification records the specification's
appearance. The requirements expressed by that specification remain distinct
from observations of the data it constrains. Similarly, a Story's declared
input, output and dependent usages remain distinct from observations in an
implementation source. Observations never create those declarations.
Statement positions identify the usage role a Story analysis expects; the
[Story Ontology](https://ekgf.org/ontology/story#) compares that evidence with
the declared usages and reports gaps as warnings. See the
[sightings guide](https://github.com/EKGF/ekg-ontologies/blob/main/docs/manifestation-sightings.md).
"""@en .

:foundIn annotation:markdownDescription """
## The artifacts containing a sighting

Links an occurrence to each artifact in which it was sighted: a dataset, a
dataset file, a statement template, a story implementation, a raw-data view,
a code file or another identified source artifact. Assert the levels the
harvester has resolved. One sighting in a statement template can be found in
the template, in the story implementation using it, and in the dataset
containing the template's file. Querying `foundIn` for a dataset then finds
both column sightings and statement sightings, while the manifestation class
and `statementPosition` distinguish how the concept appears in each.

Values are IRIs or blank nodes representing artifacts. They are not
occurrences, concepts, manifestations or statement positions; containment
between occurrences uses `occursWithin`. The property is not functional: an
occurrence can be found in several containing artifacts at different
granularities. Paths, lines and columns remain literals locating the sighting
within an artifact. A harvester must resolve artifact identity explicitly;
matching paths do not establish that two sightings share an artifact.
"""@en .

:statementPosition annotation:markdownDescription """
## How an appearance is used within a statement

Classifies a position of an occurrence within the query or update statement,
or the statement template rendering one, identified through `foundIn`:

| Position | Appearance | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ParameterPosition` | A value supplied for the invocation. | A template placeholder, or a variable the service pre-binds. |
| `ProjectionPosition` | A result the statement returns. | A projected `SELECT` variable or alias. |
| `GraphTemplatePosition` | A term the statement constructs or inserts. | A predicate in a `CONSTRUCT` or `INSERT` template. |
| `GraphPatternPosition` | A term matched against data. | A class or predicate in the `WHERE` clause. |

One appearance can have several positions. A placeholder used in a triple
pattern is a parameter appearing in the graph pattern; record both. Record
the parameter position from the template language or the service's documented
binding profile, never from a token's spelling: SPARQL treats `$name` and
`?name` as one variable.

A positioned occurrence must identify at least one artifact through `foundIn`.
Positions are evidence about a statement. They do not declare a story's concept
usages; the Story Ontology maps each position to the usage role it leads an
analysis to expect.
"""@en .

:StatementPosition annotation:markdownDescription """
## An extensible classification of statement positions

The four built-in positions are distinct named individuals. Applications can
define more positions as IRIs with a label and a definition. A position
compared with Story declarations must also identify the usage role it implies
through `ekg-story:expectedUsageRole`.

The built-ins classify SPARQL query and update positions. They do not yet
classify terms in `DELETE` templates or `DELETE DATA`; that usage role remains
an open modeling decision, so analyzers must not record those terms as
`GraphTemplatePosition`.
"""@en .

:OccurrenceSightingShape annotation:markdownDescription """
## Validate sighting artifacts and positions

Targets subjects of `foundIn` and `statementPosition`, which must be
ManifestationOccurrences and not concepts or manifestations. Artifact values
must be resources other than occurrences, concepts, manifestations and
positions. Position values must be StatementPosition IRIs. An occurrence with a
statement position must identify at least one artifact. RDFS inference supplies
occurrence and position types from the property domains and ranges; without
inference, supply those types explicitly.

The shape checks the supplied graph. It does not read source files or prove
that the asserted artifacts and positions match the source.
"""@en .

:StatementPositionShape annotation:markdownDescription """
## Validate position definitions

Targets declared positions and every object of `statementPosition`. A position
must be an IRI with a nonempty label and a nonempty definition in `rdfs:comment`
or `markdownDescription`, and must not also be a concept, manifestation or
occurrence. Load the Concept Ontology as the ontology graph to supply the
built-in definitions.
"""@en .

:OccurrenceContainmentShape annotation:markdownDescription """
## Validate the observed containment graph

Targets subjects and objects of `occursWithin`, including untyped endpoints.
Endpoints must be IRI or blank-node ManifestationOccurrences and must not also
be DataElementConcepts or ConceptManifestations. RDFS inference with the Concept
Ontology supplies endpoint types from the property's domain and range. Without
inference, supply those occurrence types explicitly.

A SPARQL property-path constraint rejects self-links and longer containment
cycles without adding transitive property semantics. Roots without a container,
multiple children and multiple direct parents remain valid. This validator and
its nested constraints belong to the Concept ValidationShapeSet.

The shape validates supplied graph structure. It does not inspect source files,
infer containment from coordinates, enforce source-provenance equality or check
harvest completeness. An analyzer must supply observed same-context edges.
"""@en .
